    \centering
    \includegraphics[width=0.9\linewidth]{p2.pdf}
    \caption{An interval layout and its corresponding interval graph}
    \label{fig:pic2}\vspace{-0.1in}
\end{figure}

In this section,  we provide a dynamic programming algorithm for computing a maximum dominating $k$-set in unit interval graphs, where each interval in the set $\cal I$ has the same length. Here, for each pair of intervals $v_i,v_j\in V$, their corresponding intervals in $\cal I$ are either disjoint or are properly overlapping (none of them is properly contained in the other interval). See Figure \ref{fig:pic3} for an example of a unit interval graph.

