\section{$\v$-numbers of integral closures of complete intersection ideals}\label{section4}
In this section, we investigate the $\v$-numbers  associated to integral closure filtrations of complete intersection ideals and analyze their relationship with the Castelnuovo-Mumford regularity of those ideals. We start with the following result which holds for any homogeneous ideals and generalizes the result \cite[Corollary 3.8]{GSV}.
\begin{Lemma}{\label{G}}
	Let $I$ be a homogeneous ideal ideal in $S$. Then $\displaystyle\lim\limits_{n\to\infty}\frac{\alpha(\overline{I^n})}{n}=\alpha(I)$.
	\end{Lemma}	
	\begin{proof}
Note that $\alpha(\overline{I^n})\leq \alpha({I^n})=n\alpha({I})$ for all $n\geq 1$. Now by \cite{MRK} and \cite[Theorem 3.2]{AS}, we have $$\displaystyle\alpha({I})\leq \lim\limits_{n\to\infty}\frac{\v(\overline{I^n})}{n}=\lim\limits_{n\to\infty}\frac{\alpha(\overline{I^n})}{n}\leq\lim\limits_{n\to\infty}\frac{n\alpha({I})}{n}=\alpha(I).$$
		\end{proof}
