Based on Theorem \ref{gen}, we focus on explicit computation of $\v$-numbers of the integral closure filtrations of $\height 3$ irreducible monomial ideals. We begin by proving the following result.
	\begin{Proposition}\label{monomialofvint}
		Let $I=\langle x_{i_1}^{a_1},x_{i_2}^{a_2},x_{i_3}^{a_3}\rangle$ be a monomial ideal in $S$ such that $1\leq a_1\leq a_2\leq a_3$. For all $1\leq m\leq a_1$, consider the monomials, $$\displaystyle {\huge {f_{m}=x_{i_1}^{a_1-m}x_{i_2}^{\lceil\frac{ma_2}{a_1}\rceil-1}x_{i_3}^{\lceil\frac{a_3}{a_2}(\frac{ma_2}{a_1}-\lceil\frac{ma_2}{a_1}\rceil+1)\rceil-1}\in S}}.$$ Then $(\overline{I}:f_m)=\langle x_{i_1},x_{i_2},x_{i_3}\rangle$ for all $1\leq m\leq a_1$. 
	\end{Proposition}
	\begin{proof}
		Let $P=\langle x_{i_1},x_{i_2},x_{i_3}\rangle$. Without loss of generality, assume that $x_{i_j}=x_j$ for all $1\leq j\leq 3$.  We first show that for all $1\leq i\leq 3$ and $1\leq m\leq a_1$, $f_m x_i\in\overline{I}$. 
		\\Note that $\displaystyle0<\frac{ma_2}{a_1}-\lceil\frac{ma_2}{a_1}\rceil+1$ implies $\displaystyle\lceil\frac{a_3}{a_2}(\frac{ma_2}{a_1}-\lceil\frac{ma_2}{a_1}\rceil+1)\rceil\geq 1$. Thus for $i=1,2$,   \begin{eqnarray*}
			&& \frac{a_1-m}{a_1}+\frac{1}{a_2}(\lceil\frac{ma_2}{a_1}\rceil-1)+\frac{1}{a_i}+\frac{1}{a_3}(\lceil\frac{a_3}{a_2}(\frac{ma_2}{a_1}-\lceil\frac{ma_2}{a_1}\rceil+1)\rceil-1)\\ &\geq& 1-\frac{m}{a_1}+\frac{1}{a_2}(\frac{ma_2}{a_1})-\frac{1}{a_2}+\frac{1}{a_i}= 1-\frac{1}{a_2}+\frac{1}{a_i}\geq 1
