\end{itemize}
%
Furthermore, \citeauthor{il81} published the ICS PAS Report 446  ``The relational model and cylindric algebras'' \cite{il81}. In December 1981 an ICS PAS Report (427) \cite{ICS427} was published of which Part 1 lists a bibliography on the theory of information systems initiated by Zdzis\l{}aw Pawlak and the first author of the present note.

From the logic point of view the modal logic \textbf{S5} is an adequate abstract framework which provides both Hilbert style axioms and  frame semantics (also referred to as possible world semantics) for the class of rough sets.

In the following years a number of papers on applications of rough sets and generalizations of the concept of rough set were published. It is now a thriving area of computer science.

