\centering
\includegraphics[width=0.8\linewidth]{photomolecularfigure0.png}
\caption{Illustrated schematics of the microscopic mechanism behind the photomolecular effect. Sharp electric field gradients of interfacial light generate enhanced cluster-photon interactions with amplitude $\sD^{\alpha\beta}_{\bm \epsilon,\bm q}$, allowing a single photon to vaporize an entire water cluster. The water cluster size distribution function $W_n$ plays an important role in generating the evaporation peak at green wavelengths.}
\label{fig0}
