\textbf{Integrated multi-angle sensing and multi-user communication:}
The near-field beam squint effect naturally provides directional frequency multiplexing for sensing and communications. As beams generated by different subcarriers are directed toward distinct spatial locations, it could simultaneously serve multiple UEs and multi-angle sensing \cite{BS3}.
