In practical applications, range measurements between sensors contain measurement error. Consequently, the measured distance matrices $\hat{E}_{P_T}$ and $\hat{E}_{P_B}$ belong to $(\mathbb{R}^{n\times n}_{+}\cap\mathbb{S}^{n}_{h})$ but may not qualify as true EDM matrices. To estimate the target state for a sensor and an agent, we employ the following systematic procedures.
